WEBVTT

00:00:00.052 --> 00:00:02.084
Press Tab. The menu won't open.

00:00:03.052 --> 00:00:04.994
Turn on the Curb Cut Chrome extension.

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:07.288
Same keys. Now the menu opens.

00:00:08.552 --> 00:00:15.869
For millions of people, this is the web. Menus that only work with a mouse. Buttons with no name. Text too faint to read.

00:00:15.944 --> 00:00:21.077
95.9 percent of the top million home pages have barriers like these.

00:00:22.052 --> 00:00:26.245
Websites take years to fix them. The people shut out can't wait that long.

00:00:27.552 --> 00:00:30.238
Curb Cut fixes them now, right in your browser.

00:00:31.552 --> 00:00:35.584
A screen reader used to say just, button. Now it says, previous slide.

00:00:36.552 --> 00:00:38.041
Faint text, made readable.

00:00:39.552 --> 00:00:50.919
And no fix ships on a guess. Kane, an AI tester, tries the task the way a disabled person would. Without the fix, it fails. With the fix, it passes. That recording is the proof.

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:56.036
105 fixes are live today, and every one shows its proof.

00:00:57.052 --> 00:01:03.644
On sites we've never seen, Jev names unlabelled buttons in about a second. When it isn't sure, it stays quiet.

00:01:04.552 --> 00:01:08.168
Then the fix goes to the site owner, so one day, nobody needs us.

00:01:09.052 --> 00:01:11.932
Curb Cut. Fixing the web for the people it shuts out.

00:01:12.007 --> 00:01:13.409
Get Curb Cut for Chrome.
